---
 33god-platform/aperture/mirror/PLAN.md | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/33god-platform/aperture/mirror/PLAN.md b/33god-platform/aperture/mirror/PLAN.md
index 9ea1d5b..9115998 100644
--- a/33god-platform/aperture/mirror/PLAN.md
+++ b/33god-platform/aperture/mirror/PLAN.md
@@ -175,6 +175,17 @@ Decision 5 is binding: same stack, CLI, hooks and bank rules as big-chungus, wit
 >   - Fix: Jarad shares the big-chungus machine with Damian in the Tailscale admin console, and Damian accepts.
 >   - Check from the Mac: `nc -z -G 5 big-chungus.burro-salmon.ts.net 7733`.
 >
+> **SUPERSEDED 2026-11-14 — owner chose a native macOS port over (c).** Pairing to big-chungus is dropped: latency kills live transcription and Damian's audio would leave his network. New target:
+> - **Mac Studio (headless):** native `vinyld serve` + `waxd` on Apple Silicon, launchd via `brew services`, CPU first.
+> - **MacBook Pro:** `vinyl-client` + HeyMa tray (cask), `vinyl setup --server damians-mac-studio:7733`, with a per-client token minted on the Studio.
+> - **Distribution:** everything ships through `delorenj/tap`. The new formula(e) for the server and Wax sit next to `vinyl-client` and the `heyma` cask.
+> - **Then:** absorb Orca's Parakeet v3 live-transcription work into Vinyl, and backfill the Linux build from the Mac work.
+> - **Feasibility proof (Studio, M3 Ultra, 96 GB, macOS 26.3):** sherpa-onnx (PyPI wheel, arm64) + `sherpa-onnx-nemo-parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v3-int8`, `provider=cpu`, 4 threads.
+>   - Model load: 0.7 s. Real-time factor 0.025, about 40x realtime. English and German transcripts came out exact.
+>   - CoreML was slower (RTF 0.06–0.13, 4.7 s load), so CPU is the default.
+>   - Vinyl's upstream recognizer is already sherpa-onnx Parakeet, so the work is packaging and launchd, not new inference.
+> - **BLOCKER:** Damian's GitHub account (DamiMiller) cannot see `delorenj/vinyl` and has pull-only on `delorenj/HeyMa`, `delorenj/homebrew-tap` and `delorenj/33GOD`. The port can't land until write access is granted or the HeyMa lane does the work.
+>
 > *Original question:* under the one-33GOD-per-network rule Damian's HeyMa should not depend on big-chungus, but Wax + the Vinyl server have no Mac port. Options: (a) Damian's client pairs to big-chungus's server — requires sharing its pairing token, which is that server's ONLY auth (lane flags this), and his audio leaves his network; (b) port vinyld/waxd to macOS (Apple Silicon transcription, launchd) as a HeyMa-lane epic, Damian's dictation waits; (c) (a) now with a per-client token added to the Vinyl server first, then (b). Recommended: (c).
 
